<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<chapter xml:id="ch-policies" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>UK Policies, Syllabi, TA Evals</title>

  <p>
    <alert>Pre-class activity</alert>: None
  </p>

  <p>
    Today is more of a "business" day, in that we will be discussing various policies that are important.
    You probably received training about a lot of these during your university orientation, but we want to return to them now that you have actively started teaching, as new questions or comments might arise. 
  </p>

  <p>
    For each of these policies, we will open the website and go through both what the policies are and what resources are available to you as instructors.
  </p>

  <p>
    <alert>FERPA, <url href="https://registrar.uky.edu/ferpa"/></alert>.
    One important point to make about FERPA in addition to what is on the website: you must use your official UKY email and OneDrive for all communication and records related to your teaching.
    Using gmail, hotmail, dropbox, google drive, etc., for storing student data is a FERPA violation.
    It is fine for you to store your teaching materials, such as your personal course notes or activity sheets, on non-UKY systems.
    However, any student data or interactions with students must be handled via UKY systems.
  </p>  
  
  <p>
    <alert>UKY Ombud, <url href="https://ombud.uky.edu/"/></alert>. 
    It is important to be aware of the academic integrity process given on the Ombud page.
  </p>

  <p>
    <alert>UKY Academic Policies, <url href="https://provost.uky.edu/academic-affairs-operations/academic-student-policies"/></alert>.
    This is the website that has links to the official UKY regulations regarding academic policies. 
    This is where all of the official rules and regulations can be found.
    (This is good to have bookmarked both as a TA and as a student yourself.)
  </p>

  <p>
    <alert>Academic alerts, <url href="https://studentsuccess.uky.edu/academic-advising/faculty-resources"/></alert>
  </p>

  <p>
    <alert>UKY TRACS, <url href="https://studentsuccess.uky.edu/tracs"/></alert>. 
    If you or one of your students is experiencing a crisis of any kind, TRACS is the first place to go.
  </p>

  <p>
    <alert>Center for Support and Intervention, <url href="https://studentsuccess.uky.edu/center-support-and-intervention"/></alert>
  </p>

  <p>
    <alert>VIP Center, <url href="https://studentsuccess.uky.edu/vip-center"/></alert>
  </p>

  <p>
    <alert>Counseling Center, <url href="https://studentsuccess.uky.edu/counseling-center"/></alert>.
    The standard recommendation is to recommend that students contact TRACS rather than the counseling center, as TRACS can help students route to multiple resources on campus. 
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <alert>Disability resource center, <url href="https://studentsuccess.uky.edu/disability-resource-center"/></alert>
  </p>

  <p>
    In addition to all of these resources, there are multiple requirements for course syllabi.
    If you are a recitation leader, then your course coordinator will handle this for most things.
    However, if you are teaching as a primary instructor, you will need to make sure that your syllabus meets all the requirements listed in the academic policies: <url href="https://provost.uky.edu/academic-affairs-operations/academic-student-policies/syllabus"/>
  </p>

  <p>
    Regarding TA evaluations, you will be evaluated twice each semester.
    First, you will be observed by a faculty member and they will fill out an evaluation form based on that observation; you will receive a copy of this form.
    Second, your course coordinator or TA supervisor will fill out an end-of-semester TA evaluation form.
    This second form is primarily focused on professionalism rather than in-class teaching performance.
  </p>


</chapter>